# YT6 — Operational Invariants Zone (Condensed Block 041–050)

1. Invariants — the non‑changing clarity constants that define system identity.
2. Boundaries — the non‑crossable operational edges that prevent drift.
3. Conditions — the must‑remain‑true requirements that anchor stability.
4. Failure Modes — deterministic breakdown behaviours when invariants are stressed.
5. Recovery — the initial return‑to‑stability behaviour after partial violation.
6. Restoration — the full return‑to‑integrity behaviour that re‑establishes baseline.
7. Reinforcement — the strengthening of invariant resilience after restoration.
8. Hardening — the increase in rigidity and resistance under repeated load.
9. Fortification — the embedding of long‑term, enterprise‑grade invariant strength.
10. Sustainment — the preservation of invariant integrity across time and environments.
